# Porto Features — PR review (agents)

**Full rules:** [`.cursor/BUGBOT.md`](../BUGBOT.md) — follow all **blocking** rules when editing `.feature` files, fixtures, or validators.

**Layering:** [features-layering-doctrine.mdc](features-layering-doctrine.mdc) · **Docs:** `docs/vocabulary.md` · `docs/scenario-policy.md` · `docs/matrix.md` · `docs/catalog-alignment.md`

## Blocking checks (summary)

1. Gherkin stays SDK-agnostic — no classes, modules, or framework internals.
2. No step definitions in this repo — SDK repos only.
3. Published assets under `porto_features/features/` and `porto_features/fixtures/` only.
4. Every Feature tagged `@sdk` or `@adapters` (exactly one).
5. SDK product input uses `porto_id` buckets (`small`, `medium`, `large`, `extra_large`) — not legacy `letter_*` / enum names.
6. No stale porto-data references (`data_links.json`, `letter_standard`, etc.) — use current bundle layout.

Non-blocking: validator updates, fixture scope, readability, changelog, tracked TODOs.
